# Every variable this site reads, with where to obtain it. The real values live
# encrypted in .env.production (Netlify production build); set one with
# `npx dotenvx set KEY value -f .env.production`, which encrypts it.
#
# Only VITE_* keys reach the browser bundle. Vite's own .env loading is pointed
# away from the repo root (envDir in .vitepress/config.ts), so they arrive
# solely through `dotenvx run`, never as ciphertext read from a committed file.

# Sentry — https://sentry.io → Settings → Projects → your project → Client Keys (DSN)
# Set only in .env.production, so local, CI and Deploy Preview builds report
# nothing to Sentry and skip the source map upload.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0
#
# Source map upload at build time. Auth token: https://sentry.io → Settings →
# Auth Tokens (org token with project:releases + org:read). Org and project are
# the slugs in your Sentry URL.
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=sntrys_...
# SENTRY_ORG=neonpixels
# SENTRY_PROJECT=grimicorn
